From 073a0e09c73f5ead160fc29a541d420ae64bb9d4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Thu, 2 Jul 2026 10:28:08 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 05482/11362] [outer-loop] un-quarantine exp5161's GAP-4 pilot:
 substrate mislabel, not fabrication

Operator: 'dig into the GAP-4 DURATION_TOO_SHORT flag' -> 'Fix this, correct
the substrate declaration and un-quarantine it.'

results/experiment_5161_gap4_protocol_execution_pilot_v473.json was FLAGGED
CRITICAL (DURATION_TOO_SHORT, 5.59s vs a 60s live_llm_inference floor) and
quarantined. Investigated before touching it: the artifact's dominant
content (n=60 pilot statistics rescoring GAP-4's existing cached candidate
pool, cluster bootstrap, exact sign test) does not invoke a generative LLM
-- duration_s=5.59s is genuinely implausible for live_llm_inference but
plausible for cached-candidate rescoring.

Root cause: inference_substrate was a {principle, value} dict, which
adversarial_verify.py's _inference_substrate_text() cannot parse (str() on
a dict produces a Python repr matching no canonical value), so the
duration-floor check fell through to the generic compute-bound-marker
fallback (60s) regardless of what substrate was actually declared -- this
affected the ORIGINAL declaration too, meaning the flag never really
tested substrate recognition in the first place.

Fixed: corrected inference_substrate to a bare string (matching
_inference_substrate_matches()'s documented canonical-value-plus-separator
convention). Added model_specs/target_model reflecting the one model
genuinely invoked (a single local-generator-arm cache-availability smoke
call, ~5.57s of the 5.59s total -- an identity-function response, not
GAP-4's real decentralization-tier requirement, documented as an honest
open caveat, not silently dropped). Independently reverified the remaining
INFO flag (exact_test_discordant_losses=0.0) via
scipy.stats.binomtest(4, 4, 0.5) -- recomputes to exactly 0.125, matching
the artifact's own declared p-value, confirming the pilot stats are real,
not a stub.

flagged_adversarial now false, live re-check clean (0 CRITICAL flags).
Updated ops/verifier_gaps.md's GAP-4 entry with the real result: direction
replicates at n=60 (4 discordant wins, 0 losses, p=0.125), short of the
protocol's own >=6-win significance floor; decentralization tier and
400-task scale-up both still genuinely open.

Flagged, not fixed: found 176 artifacts corpus-wide share this exact
{principle, value}-dict inference_substrate structure, meaning
adversarial_verify.py's substrate recognition has been silently defeated
for all of them regardless of declared value. That's a separate, larger
decision (fix the linter to accept both forms vs. leave as-is) than this
task's scope -- reported in ops/known-issues.md, not acted on.

